Z||000000||Seanh||11-27-2001||09:33 AM||||I just can't put up with this anymore...Last night my $550 stereo is stolen from the car, now this morning I started the car and was letting it warm up, but when I when to the car about 5 min later I thought it wierd there was absolutly no heat yet, so I just put my gloves on and took off in the car, few miles later, still no heat and the temp guage is climbing...I got the hint and pulled into a parking lot before it overheats again...(it got up to 220 and climbing)...So I got a rag and loosened the thermo state cap, and let alot of presuure out...After the pressure had excaped I removed the cap completly and found no coolant. Pulled the stat and no coolant under it either. Started the engine and no coolant was splashing out of the housing...So what is this telling me? I can pretty much guess your going to say its a bad water pump, but could it be somthing else (hopefully)? (Well, as long as its not a cracked block) So what are your thoughts? I have to be at an appointment at 915 so I got a ride back home and I'll take off and work on the car afterwards...Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly - 86 GT<BR>Back to my 3.1L...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image2.gif"> ||||reg||9
