Z||000003||84Bill||11-27-2001||10:21 AM||||LOL <BR>I'm laughing with you not at you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>Could be a lot worse, Like overheated with a flat tire and a stripped lugnut and to top it off when you strike your last match to burn the car and the matchhead pops off wedges under a fingernail and ignites. After a 6 hour wait your ride shows up to take you home 10 minutes later your car is marked abandoned then towed to some unknown location.||||reg||12
Z||000004||Rumor||11-27-2001||10:33 AM||||Sorry to hear about the Stereo. Here's a story that I tell anyone who has had their stereo stolen :<P>There was a guy who went to his car, and found the window smashed, and his stereo stolen. He installed a second one, and once again, his found his window smashed, his stereo gone. He went out and bought a third stereo, this time a REALLY expensive one, and installed it in his car and repaired the window a third time.  The easiest way to remove the stereo was to reach underneeath, and push forward against the heat-sink on the back of the radio. The guy crazy-glued razorblades (the REALLY thin double-sided ones)onto the heat-sink fins on the back of the radio. Two mornings later, when the guy came up to his car, It had a broken window and the door was left open slightly. there was a scattered trail of red leading away from the car.  When he looked inside, he saw the radio, half-pushed out, and a puddle of blood on the passenger-side floor. He never had his stereo stolen again...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||11-27-2001||07:11 PM||||Well, I'v got bad news but not the worst news (I think) I filled it up, and started the car without the thermostat or cap in/on. It didn't spew any coolant and I couldn't even see any moving around...So I'm assume the water pump is shot right? I bought a new one today with a metal impeller and am going to start on it tonight, so how long do you think somthing like this will take? Thanks||||reg||1
