Z||000007||Swany||11-27-2001||07:23 PM||||are you sure its the water pump?.. did ya check the heater core? <P>When my heater core went out it acted very similiar, would run for a little while, then the temp gauge would keep climbing. After pulling over the water lvl would be very low, after putting in around 2 gallons of water it would act normal for bout a mile. <P>Just another Idea||||reg||1
Z||000008||Seanh||11-27-2001||07:27 PM||||I could understand a loss of coolant if the heatcore went out, but there isn't any coolant cirrulating around when I run it with that thermostat removed and cap off, so i'm almost sure its the water pump. Might have a cracked block too, but I wouldn't be able to tell until I replace the water pump tomarrow...||||reg||1
Z||000009||GTDude||11-27-2001||10:09 PM||||Remember in the fiero there is a lot of water...it goes from the radiator in the front to the engine in the back.....takes a long time to get it full of coolant and get the trapped air out.  Turn the A/C on so that the coolant fan will run and fill up the radiator first.  Then go back and fill the engine.......it may take 30 min or more.  Be patient.||||reg||1
